Can ref keyword be used in Async programming? 

Yes, the ref keyword can be used in async programming starting with C# 13, but with important restrictions. Before C# 13, using ref variables across await calls was disallowed because the memory location could become invalid when execution resumed. Now, C# 13 allows ref locals in async methods, provided they are safely managed across awaits.

