What are collections and its type.
In C#, collections are specialized classes that store groups of related objects. They provide more flexibility than arrays because they can grow or shrink dynamically, and they come with built-in methods for searching, sorting, and manipulating data.
1. Non-Generic Collections
Found in System.Collections namespace.
Store objects as object type → type casting required.
Examples:
